      <p class="paraCommon paraHeader"  >    <b>Green Domains, Not Green Degrees </b>
       
      </p>
          <p class="paraCommon">Green jobs don’t ask, <i>“What did you study?”</i></p>
     <p class="paraCommon">They ask, <i>“Which problem do you care about?”</i></p>
      <p class="paraCommon">Food. Farms. Forests. Climate. Energy. Waste. Water. Cities. Communities.</p>
       <p class="paraCommon">These are <b>domains</b>, not degrees.</p>
        <p class="paraCommon">A commerce student can work in carbon markets.</p>
   <p class="paraCommon">An arts graduate can work in climate communication.</p>
   <p class="paraCommon">An ITI student can work in solar maintenance.</p>
 <p class="paraCommon">A science student can work in food safety or soil health.</p>
 <p class="paraCommon">Same domain. Different entry points.</p>
 <p class="paraCommon">If you can understand the problem and learn what’s needed around it, you’re in.</p>
 
 
  
